za","strFacebook":"www.facebook.com\/OfficialPSL\/","strInstagram":"","strTwitter":"twitter.com\/officialpsl","strYoutube":"","strRSS":"","strDescriptionEN":"The South African Premiership, also known as the Betway Premiership for sponsorship reasons, and commonly referred to as the PSL after its governing body, is a professional soccer league in South Africa and the highest level of the South African soccer league system. It has been organised since 1996.\r\n\r\nOrlando Pirates F.C. are the current champions, winning the 2025–26 South African Premiership, breaking Mamelodi Sundowns' eight year winning streak. This marked their fifth league title in the PSL era and their 10th overall. This also marks their first league title since the 2011–12 season.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strTvRights":"","strFanart1":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/fanart\/8w6un71716215721.jpg","strFanart2":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/fanart\/9ajg461716215726.jpg","strFanart3":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/fanart\/kbvzvp1716215752.jpg","strFanart4":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/fanart\/wjy1281716216094.jpg","strBanner":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/banner\/70uvad1638919448.jpg","strBadge":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/badge\/e59xj11725174551.png","strLogo":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/logo\/ygkj481725174632.png","strPoster":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/poster\/q1epo61716216149.jpg","strTrophy":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/trophy\/niq9su1716216413.png","strNaming":"{strHomeTeam} vs {strAwayTeam}","strComplete":"yes","strLocked":"unlocked"},{"idLeague":"5197","idAPIfootball":"8627","idAPIfootballv3":"509","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"South-Africa 8 Cup","strLeagueAlternate":"MTN 8","intDivision":"99","idCup":"1","strCurrentSeason":"2026","intFormedYear":"1972","dateFirstEvent":"2021-08-14","strGender":"Male","strCountry":"South Africa","strWebsite":"","strFacebook":"","strInstagram":"","strTwitter":"","strYoutube":"","strRSS":"","strDescriptionEN":"The MTN 8 is a South African football (soccer) cup competition, featuring the top 8 clubs at the close of the previous DStv Premiership season. This competition is one of the longest-standing knockout cup competitions in South Africa, first being contested in 1972. The winner receives R8 million.\r\n\r\nThe first round is structured such that the team at the top of the previous season's table plays the team that finished eighth; second place plays seventh; third plays sixth and fourth plays fifth. The semifinals are played over two legs.\r\n\r\nCellular giants MTN have sponsored the event since 2008. Before then it was known as BP Top 8 (sponsored by BP) and SAA Supa 8 (sponsored by South African Airways).","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strTvRights":"","strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strBanner":null,"strBadge":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/league\/badge\/bw3hpu1645321585.png","strLogo":null,"strPoster":null,"strTrophy":null,"strNaming":"{strHomeTeam} vs {strAwayTeam}","strComplete":"No","strLocked":"unlocked"}]}